.TH AGENTGUARD-TELEMETRY 1 "2026-10-07" "agentguard" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agentguard-telemetry \- find, read, and prune AgentGuard audit records
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agentguard-telemetry dir
.br
.B agentguard-telemetry sessions
.RB [ \-\-agent
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-n
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B agentguard-telemetry show
.RI [ SESSION ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B agentguard-telemetry path
.RI [ SESSION ]
.br
.B agentguard-telemetry prune
.RB [ \-\-days
.IR N ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
AgentGuard hooks record what every agent session did: prompts, every tool
call with its full input and output, guard decisions, and lifecycle events.
Records live under
.I ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-~/.local/state}/agentguard/telemetry/sessions/AGENT/SESSION/
as one JSON file per hook invocation.
.B agentguard-telemetry
is the read side.
.TP
.B dir
Print the telemetry root that hooks write to.
.TP
.B sessions
List sessions with their last activity, record count, working directory,
and first prompt, newest first.
.B \-\-agent
filters by runtime,
.B \-n
limits the count (default 20, 0 for all), and
.B \-\-json
prints one JSON object per session.
.TP
.B show
Print a session's timeline, one line per record. With
.BR \-\-json ,
print the raw records as JSONL for
.BR jq (1).
.TP
.B path
Print a session's record directory.
.TP
.B prune
Delete sessions idle for more than
.I N
days (default
.B AGENTGUARD_TELEMETRY_RETENTION_DAYS
or 90).
.PP
.I SESSION
is
.B latest
(the default),
.B all
(every session, for
.B show
only),
.B current
(the agent session running the command, from its runtime session
variables), an exact
.IR AGENT / KEY
or
.IR KEY ,
a unique key prefix, or a session directory path. For Claude Code the key
is the session UUID that also names its transcript.
.PP
When
.B AGENTGUARD_TELEMETRY_DIR
is an absolute path, it is the only root searched or pruned. Otherwise
readers merge the
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
root and
.IR ~/.local/state ,
because some runtimes scrub
.B XDG_*
variables from hook environments.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
No matching session, an ambiguous prefix, or no records.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
agentguard-telemetry show current
agentguard-telemetry show 8a15fead \-\-json |
  jq \-r 'select(.event=="PreToolUse") | .payload.tool_input.command // empty'
rg \-l 'rm \-rf' "$(agentguard-telemetry dir)"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR agent-hook-telemetry (1)
